  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 140 AM MDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nToday through Wed night...The upper level ridge centered over \nthe desert southwest will strengthen over the next couple of \ndays. This will put temperatures on a very weak warming trend, \nbut it will not stop moist and unstable air rotating through the\nupper level southwest flow into southern Idaho. SPC has once \nagain put the southern 2/3 of the forecast area in an area of \nmarginal severe thunderstorm threat. Fortunately, this marginal \nthreat is only expected to last through this evening. Weaker \nthunderstorms with lessening threat continues Tue through Thu, \nthen beyond this the threat falls off even more. Wind outside of\nthunderstorms should return to being light. \n\nThu through Sun...As mentioned above, the trend is for less and\nless thunderstorm activity, barely rating mentioning during this\nperiod. However, on Thu this upper level ridge breaks down as\nthe coastal upper level low pushes onshore in southern Canada.\nThis movement causes the airflow to be more westerly and drier,\nand the incoming low increases the gradient aloft as it makes\nits closest approach on Thu, Fri, and Sat afternoons, when the \nstronger wind gets a chance to mix down to the surface. The\napproach of this low also produces a cooling trend that starts\nThu afternoon to the end of the forecast period.",
